gence, in less than an Olympic cycle, of a strong East German bobsleigh programme. Formed with a backbone of converted track and field athletes the GDR had threatened to break through to the podium positions over the previous seasons and in Innsbruck this was achieved in spectacular fashion. The reigning world champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/97370"} "Erich Schärer"] ", driving Switzerland II, reined in the gap on the second day of competition but " [:a {:href "/athletes/95777"} "Manfred Nehmer"] "’s GDR I bob had built up too much of an advantage to be overhauled in the contest for gold. Nehmer began only the second man to secure victory in both events at the same Games and the first to do so at his début Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {} "Run #3"] [:th {} "Run #4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "East Germany 1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "3:40.43"] [:td {} "54.43 (1)"] [:td {} "54.64 (1)"] [:td {} "55.51 (2)"] [:td {} "55.85 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "13"} [:a {:href "/athletes/95777"} "Meinhard Nehmer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/83771"} "Jochen Babock"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/86027"} "Bernhard Germeshausen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/89525"} "Bernhard Lehmann"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Switzerland 2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "3:40.89"] [:td {} "54.96 (5)"] [:td {} "54.81 (2)"] [:td {} "55.28 (1)"] [:td {} "55.84 (1)"